<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bigbury Camp</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bigbury Camp is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> in Kent, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, covering about 10 hectares. It is probably the stronghold that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s Seventh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> stormed in 54 BCE, and finds from it include iron tools, slave chains and horse gear. It was later replaced as the regional centre by the oppidum at Canterbury.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bigbury-camp.jpg" alt="Bigbury Camp" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Doyle of London · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slope_at_the_Northeast_Area_of_Bigbury_Camp_(01).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
